      ", on surface.canvas). It decorates, so it holds no contrast minimum."
     ],
     "darkPick": [
      "neutral.300: We use the step above the raised surface for dividers and card borders in dark in order to give separation on every surface a line meets, menus included. The line does this by staying lighter than each surface, lowest ",
      {
       "ratio": 1.8
      },
      ", on surface.raised. So rows and cards stay apart on content and in menus, because lines separate groups (elevation.definition) and dark ships as standard (theming.values)."
